  "_notes": [
    "pendingConfirmation is null and the lines are unchanged: the flip does not move the plant, so it does not re-price. A server that raises a storeChange confirm here has implemented §2.2 wrong.",
    "plant and plantSource are RETAINED across the flip — that IS how the plant got there. This is also the open question 154 records: plantSource now does double duty and has no value meaning 'chosen for pickup'.",
    "\uD83D\uDEA9 v1.8 (877 §2.6): header.retainedAddressLabel carries the LABEL of the held address — \"Home\", \"Work\" — and NEVER the address line, city or district. Non-null exactly under PickInStore with an address on the sidecar, cleared on the flip back. It exists because the flip back re-derives the plant from that address and can raise a §5.1 storeChange confirmation about a store the agent never chose, on an order that has shown them no address for ten minutes. A console that remembered the last address IT saw was built and rejected (owner ruling 2026-07-29): blank after a refresh, blank in a second tab, blank on a resumed order.",
    "header.address is null but the address is RETAINED in the CallCenterSession sidecar. Flipping back to Delivery restores it without re-keying and re-derives the plant through setAddress's existing confirm path. A server that clears it is the second likely mis-implementation.",
    "submitBlockers drops NO_ADDRESS and MISSING_SLOT: neither applies to a pickup order.",
    "deliveryFee.amount is 0 by the predicate that already exists for the CallCenterOrder doctype (786's CallCenterDeliveryFeePolicy, extracted from POSController.NewPos.cs), not by a new rule — and waived stays FALSE, because a fee that never existed was not waived. thresholdGross is still quoted because the threshold is real."
  ]
}
